814 0 obj
  << /ActualText (About me\nUX\057UI Designer with a background in Visual Communication\056 \nExpert in characterizing and designing B2B products\054 complex systems\054 and brand assets\054 focusing on business goals and conversion \050CRO\051\056 Possesses expertise in building comprehensive design systems\054 leveraging AI tools\054 and making digital interfaces accessible in accordance with strict standards and organizational goals\056\n\nExperience\nUX\057UI Designer \174 Freelance   \0502023 \055 2026\051\nLed end\055to\055end \050E2E\051 characterization and design processes for responsive websites\054 portals\054 dashboards\054 and complex systems for a variety of clients\056\nManaged direct workflows with developers \050Hand\055off\051\054 product managers\054 and organizational stakeholders\054 while maintaining business goals and an intuitive user experience\056\nConducted user research\054 built personas\054 information architecture\054 wireframes\054 and complex prototypes to identify and solve pain points in digital work environments\056\nOptimized conversion rates \050CRO\051\054 refined user flows\054 and simplified digital forms to reduce friction\056\n\nProjects\nBianca \174 B2B Restaurant Management Dashboard   \0502026\051\nLed the full design cycle of a B2B system\054 including competitor analysis\054 prototyping\054 and building a scalable Design System to optimize complex workflows\056\nAnalyzed operational bottlenecks and optimized workflows in complex management interfaces\056\nTesi \174 EdTech Landing Page \046 CRO  \0502025\051\nDesigned responsive interfaces \050Web \046 Mobile\051 with a focus on improving conversion rates \050CRO\051 and engagement\056\nApplied data\055driven design to refine user flows\054 reducing friction and significantly improving onboarding and conversion rates \050CRO\051\056\n\nEDUCATION\nOpen University of Israel   \0502020 \055 2023\051\nB\056A\056 in Visual Communication\n\nProg College   \0502024\051\nUX\057UI Design)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 815 0 R
     /Pg 810 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
